-<section id="page-settings" class="page" aria-label="Settings"><div class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow dark">PRIVATE BY DESIGN</span><h2>Make it yours.</h2><p>Your Google Sheet remains the master source. Connect for read-only refreshes, with a saved copy for offline use.</p></div>
- <div class="panel theme-panel"><h3>Appearance</h3><p>Modern Imperial China, in your light.</p><label class="field" for="themeSelect"><span>Choose your theme</span><select id="themeSelect"><option value="light">Light · Porcelain ivory</option><option value="dark">Dark · Lacquer black</option></select></label><p class="caption" id="themeStatus" role="status">Light is the default. Your selection stays on this device.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Private Google Sheet sync</h3>
- <p>Connect your Google account to read your existing tracker. Other trip tabs stay read-only. Packing & Bags writes require separate opt-in file authorization.</p>
- <details><summary>Google OAuth setup</summary><label class="field"><span>Existing private workbook URL or ID</span><input id="googleSheetId" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Paste your existing tracker URL locally"></label><button class="secondary-btn" id="saveTrackerConfig">Save existing tracker</button><label class="field" for="googleClientId"><span>Public OAuth web client ID</span><input id="googleClientId" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="…apps.googleusercontent.com"></label><p class="caption">Saved only on this device. A client ID is public configuration; never enter a client secret, password or token.</p></details>
- <div class="button-row"><button class="primary-btn" id="googleConnect">Connect Google</button><button class="secondary-btn" id="googleSyncNow" disabled>Refresh now</button></div>
- <div class="notice" id="googleSyncState" role="status" aria-live="polite">Google Cloud OAuth setup pending. Your offline data is safe.</div>
- <p class="caption">Refreshes every 5 minutes while the app is open and authorized, and when you return or reconnect. After authorization expires or the app reloads, tap Connect Google again. Google services may be unreachable in China; refresh and check your offline copy before departure.</p>
- <div class="button-row"><button class="secondary-btn" id="googleDisconnect">Disconnect session</button><button class="secondary-btn" id="googleRevoke">Revoke Google access</button></div>
- <p class="caption">Disconnect and revoke keep your offline copy. Use Clear below to erase saved trip data and expenses from this browser. Revoke works with a live token; otherwise remove access in your Google Account.</p>
- </div>
- <div class="panel"><h3>Google Drive receipts</h3><p>Keep all China Trip receipts in one private Google Drive folder. First enable Google Drive API and Google Picker API in your existing Cloud project; add only the <code>drive.file</code> OAuth scope.</p><details><summary>Receipt upload setup</summary><label class="field" for="receiptProjectNumber"><span>Google Cloud project number (digits)</span><input id="receiptProjectNumber" type="text" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="e.g. 123456789012" autocomplete="off"></label><label class="field" for="receiptApiKey"><span>Google Picker API key (restrict by website and API)</span><input id="receiptApiKey" type="text" autocomplete="off" placeholder="AIza…"></label><p class="caption">These public configuration values are stored only in this browser. Restrict the key to https://shaunlittmanco.github.io/* and https://docs.google.com/*, and to Google Picker API and Google Drive API. Never paste a client secret or access token.</p></details><div class="button-row"><button class="secondary-btn" id="connectReceiptDrive">Connect receipt uploads</button><button class="secondary-btn" id="disconnectReceiptDrive">Disconnect uploads</button></div><button class="secondary-btn full" id="chooseReceiptFolder">Choose Google Drive receipts folder</button><div class="notice" id="receiptDriveStatus" role="status">Receipt uploads need additional Google Drive authorization.</div><p class="caption">Choose the folder named <strong>China Trip 2027 - Receipts</strong>. Google Picker opens inside the app; access is granted only to files and folders you choose. Uploads require internet. The private Sheet sync stays read-only.</p></div>
- <div class="panel"><h3>Load your trip data</h3><p class="muted">Choose <b>china-trip-private-data.json</b> from Files. The app stores it only in this browser's local storage, without uploading it to our servers.</p><label class="file-import">Choose private JSON <input id="dataFile" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"></label><div id="importStatus" class="notice">Demo mode is active until you import your private data.</div><button id="clearData" class="danger-btn">Clear imported trip and expenses</button></div>
- <div class="panel"><h3>Install on iPhone</h3><p>After this website is published over HTTPS, open it in Safari → Share → Add to Home Screen.</p><div class="notice">You can open the included local files on a computer for inspection, but offline install/service worker requires HTTPS or localhost. GitHub Pages hosting is free for public repositories; keep the private JSON out of your repository.</div></div>
- <div class="panel"><h3>Privacy & limitations</h3><p>Imported bookings are saved in <b>localStorage</b> on your device, not encrypted. Avoid shared devices. Safari clearing website data or switching browsers will remove saved data. Export or re-import a backup.</p><p>Maps need internet, and mainland China may block some third-party tiles. Saved itinerary, phrasebook, currency math and imported bookings can work offline after first successful install.</p><p>Tracker sync uses only the read-only Google Sheets permission. Google describes this scope as viewing all your spreadsheets; this app reads only your privately configured tracker. Packing Sync separately uses file-scoped drive.file consent/Picker selection; writes are restricted by code to Packing & Bags. Access tokens stay in memory and disappear on reload. No client secret or refresh token is used. Two-way voice mode is experimental and can stop on iPhone Safari. Full reliable always-listening translation and live metro routing are not implemented.</p></div>
- <div class="panel"><h3>Version</h3><p>App 1.7.3 · Unified Packing Auto Sync + Daily Carry · published release</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Tracker source</h3><a id="trackerSourceLink" hidden target="_blank" rel="noopener">China Trip Command Center 2027 ↗</a><p class="muted" id="syncStatus">Snapshot date: 23 Oct 2026. Updates require importing another snapshot.</p></div>
